<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.2.1: Squares in a Geometric Pattern</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01757</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.2.1: Squares in a Geometric Pattern</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5a2afa81-86e9-444b-87b3-ee39af81dc15</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para>How does each expression represent the number of small squares in the figure?</para>
      <para>
          <media alt="An image of a block of squares. There are eight squares on rows 1, 2, 3 and 4 and five squares on rows 5 - 6. There are six squares missing from the upper right corner of the block.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_02_01.svg" />
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Expression A: \(6 \cdot 8−2 \cdot 3\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>There are 6 rows with 8 small squares, but from this, 2 rows of 3 small squares have been removed.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Expression B: \(4 \cdot 8+2 \cdot 5\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>There are 4 rows of 8 small squares, and to this, 2 rows of 5 small squares are added.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Expression C: \(8+8+8+8+5+5\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>This counts each row, starting from the bottom.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Expression D: \(5 \cdot 6+3 \cdot 4\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>There are 5 columns of 6 small squares and 3 columns of 4 small squares.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <note>
        <para>Building Character: Proactivity</para>
<media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_04_02_02.png" />
          </media>

            <para>Proactivity is the ability to take initiative. There’s evidence that proactivity is one of the qualities that distinguished the greatest American presidents from their peers.</para>
            <para>Think about your current sense of proactivity. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
            <list>
          <item> I am always looking for better ways of doing things. </item>
          <item> I love to challenge the status quo. </item>
        </list>
            <para>Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>